    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2TDvuJ2KygqHcBPtkDgePBK)_\n\n## What\n- After #422, `sp-reading-refresh` ran without error but said `sp-reading: 0 PDFs in literature`.\n- Most likely cause (not yet confirmed on your Mac): the listing kept only records whose **name** ends in `.pdf`, but DEVONthink often keeps a record name without the extension. The litdb indexer (which works) selects on the file **path**.\n- Fix: the listing keeps records whose **path** ends in `.pdf`, and adds `.pdf` to the name when it is missing, so the citekey is still `name` without the extension.\n- Debugging: `M-x sp-reading-diagnose` shows, in `*sp-reading diagnose*`, the open databases, the number of records, how many PDFs are found by path and by name, and a sample of PDF records (name, path, kind). `sp-reading-refresh` now says `0 PDFs in literature; run M-x sp-reading-diagnose to see why` when it finds nothing.\n- Changed in `docs/tangles/academic/sp-reading.org` and the tangled `sp-reading.el`; 9 ERT tests pass (new one: script text, empty-result message, diagnose buffer).\n\n## Not tested\n- On the Mac (I cannot run DEVONthink). If the count is still 0, the diagnose output tells which assumption is wrong (database name, records without a path, or kind).\n\n## Manual testing\n- [x] `cd ~/dotfiles; git fetch origin 426-sp-reading-path-filter; git checkout 426-sp-reading-path-filter`, restart Emacs.\n- [x] `M-x sp-reading-refresh` → \"sp-reading: N PDFs in literature\" with N about 15,000.\n- [x] If it says `0 PDFs … run M-x sp-reading-diagnose`: run `M-x sp-reading-diagnose` and paste me the buffer (databases, `records`, `pdf_by_path`, `pdf_by_name`, `sample`).\n- [ ] `M-:` `(gethash \"harrison-2010-therborn-post-marx\" sp-reading-index)` → a UUID string.\n- [x] `M-x sp-reading-open`, choose a key → the record opens in DEVONthink.\n- [ ] `M-x sp-devonthink-browse` is on the stacked PR #415 (it lists with the older name filter, which I will fix there once this is confirmed).\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiDWYwkgX4eqm2SVoTC)_",
